WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.744 --> 00:00:02.779
defending taijuan.

00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:03.913
&gt;&gt; I'll have that conversation

00:00:04.047 --> 00:00:04.347
with him.

00:00:04.481 --> 00:00:07.283
&gt;&gt; I actually have an unrelated

00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:07.750
question, too.

00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:09.319
Mr. President, do you think Elon

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:10.753
Musk is a threat to U.S.

00:00:10.887 --> 00:00:13.756
National security and should the

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:19.896
U.S. And with the tools you have

00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:20.563
investigate his joint acre

00:00:20.697 --> 00:00:22.165
acquisition with Twitter and

00:00:22.298 --> 00:00:25.802
foreign governments like the

00:00:25.935 --> 00:00:26.369
Saudis?

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:29.072
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.205 --> 00:00:38.815
&gt;&gt; I think that Elon Musk's

00:00:38.948 --> 00:00:43.887
cooperation and/or technical

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.591
relationships with other

00:00:48.725 --> 00:00:50.827
countries is worthy of being

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:51.794
looked at.

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:53.296
Whether or not he is doing

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:55.798
anything inappropriate, I'm not

00:00:55.932 --> 00:00:56.633
suggesting that.

00:00:56.766 --> 00:01:03.206
I'm suggesting at worst being

00:01:03.339 --> 00:01:06.342
looked at and -- and that's all

00:01:06.476 --> 00:01:08.478
I'll say.

00:01:08.611 --> 00:01:09.312
&gt;&gt; How?

00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:14.184
&gt;&gt; There's a lot of ways.

00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:17.820
All right.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:18.121
Kristen Welker?

00:01:18.254 --> 00:01:19.822
&gt;&gt; Thank you so much, Mr.

00:01:19.822 --> 00:01:19.989
President.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.192
I appreciate it.

00:01:22.325 --> 00:01:24.227
I want to follow up with you on

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.463
working with Republicans.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.832
Leader Mccarthy again suggested

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:31.868
that he is not prepared to write

00:01:32.001 --> 00:01:33.503
what he says a blank check to

00:01:33.836 --> 00:01:35.838
Ukraine and yet, you expressed

00:01:35.838 --> 00:01:38.841
optimism that funding for

00:01:38.975 --> 00:01:40.376
Ukraine would continue, that the

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.844
policies toward Ukraine would

00:01:41.844 --> 00:01:41.945
continue.

00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:44.047
Why should the people of Ukraine

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.848
and this country have confidence

00:01:45.848 --> 00:01:47.183
in that given the comments by

00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:48.618
leader Mccarthy and just to

00:01:48.751 --> 00:01:49.852
follow up with you on your

00:01:49.886 --> 00:01:51.854
comments to zeke, you said you

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:53.223
don't need to do anything

00:01:53.356 --> 00:01:53.856
differently.

00:01:53.856 --> 00:01:55.091
If Republicans control the

00:01:55.225 --> 00:01:57.060
house, don't you need to

00:01:57.193 --> 00:01:58.194
recalibrate to some extent to

00:01:58.328 --> 00:01:59.429
try to work across the aisle

00:01:59.862 --> 00:02:01.364
with the Republican led house?

00:02:01.497 --> 00:02:03.900
&gt;&gt; Well, let me put it this way.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.301
What I meant is I don't have to

00:02:05.435 --> 00:02:06.869
change the policies that have

00:02:07.003 --> 00:02:07.870
already passed.

00:02:07.937 --> 00:02:09.038
That's what they said they want

00:02:09.172 --> 00:02:10.106
to go after.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.076
What I have is a simple

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:13.476
proposition.

00:02:13.876 --> 00:02:15.278
I have a pen to veto.

00:02:15.411 --> 00:02:17.180
That's what I mean.

00:02:17.313 --> 00:02:18.314
I don't have to recalibrate

00:02:18.448 --> 00:02:19.882
whether I'm going to continue to

00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:21.017
fund -- we're going to continue

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.585
to fund the infrastructure bill

00:02:22.719 --> 00:02:24.854
or we're going to continue to

00:02:24.988 --> 00:02:27.457
fund the environment, et cetera.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.395
We have to -- I hope -- there is

00:02:33.162 --> 00:02:35.064
a growing pressure on the part

00:02:35.198 --> 00:02:38.935
of the American people expecting

00:02:39.068 --> 00:02:41.971
both parties and all elements of

00:02:42.105 --> 00:02:51.080
both parties to work out their

00:02:51.214 --> 00:02:52.215
substantive differences and not

00:02:52.348 --> 00:02:53.916
just -- I'm not going to do that

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.086
because it would benefit that

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:57.387
party.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.188
Just make it personal.

00:02:59.322 --> 00:03:02.158
So I -- and, you know, it

00:03:02.292 --> 00:03:03.960
remains to be seen what the

00:03:04.093 --> 00:03:07.930
makeup of the house will be but

